`xs.map(f)` and `xs.filter(f)` read in a view body, on the Go targets, which
withhold listLambdas so NoListLambdas hoists an accumulator loop ahead of the
widget reading the result.

On bubbletea a view body's `for` is a view loop, so the accumulator was
rendered as one: its body was dropped, the list stayed empty, and the widget
reading `[0]` of it panicked on the first frame. A loop whose body draws
nothing is now a statement in the view function.

fyne and gtk4 make the accumulator loop a render slot, whose function appends
to a list declared in the build function; that is not fixed here.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `part\d+Items` -- an accumulator loop is not a view loop
broken out/go/fyne -- the hoisted accumulator loop becomes a render slot, which appends to a list declared in the build function it cannot see
broken out/go/gtk4 -- the hoisted accumulator loop becomes a render slot, which appends to a list declared in the build function it cannot see
-- view.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

func dbl(x int) => x * 2

component main node {
    var xs = [3, 4]
    text(value="{xs.map(dbl)[0]} {xs.filter(func(x int) => x > 3)[0]}")
}

window {
    main
}

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}
